function txt = nm_ui_bridge_python_template()
% nm_ui_bridge_python_template  Return the Python HTTP bridge source written into each temporary NM2 UI web directory.
%
% Purpose
%   Defines the local Python transport server used by browser UIs for static assets, synchronous
%   MATLAB services, durable long-running MATLAB jobs, progress polling and session lifecycle signals.
%
% Authority and flow
%   Python owns HTTP admission and file-backed transport state only. Ordinary matlabservice requests
%   remain synchronous and timeout-protected. matlabjob submissions are acknowledged immediately,
%   persisted as queued jobs and later executed by the MATLAB dispatcher through the same operation
%   handler used by synchronous services.
%
% Invariants
%   A durable job has no wall-clock timeout in this server. While one is queued/running, additional
%   MATLAB-backed synchronous requests are rejected immediately rather than queued behind MATLAB.
%   Progress/job-status/static-file endpoints remain directly available from Python.
%   CLIENT under CLIENT_LOCK owns live controller status. The authenticated
%   diagnostic response exposes a snapshot directly; no disk liveness copy
%   is written. Stream teardown is scoped to client identity and generation.
%
% Materialization and performance
%   Running-job polling serves compact status/progress files. The scientific service result is served
%   once from its terminal result file; the Python bridge does not repeatedly serialize MATLAB state.
%
% Failure semantics
%   Ordinary synchronous services retain finite transport timeouts. Durable-job submission failures
%   are explicit; accepted jobs expose terminal failure through their status/result files.

